2	
3	Reviewed 2026-10-29 against the brief at base 36ffe5b4, with W2-01 (`spec-pipeline/protocol`), W2-01b (`ui/screen.ts`), W2-02 (`ResidueRow`), W2-04 (the fake) and W2-05 (`run/ir.ts`) as their briefs leave them. tools/dpf is not registered for lint until W2-01b, so every block was linted at `tools/scripts/__probe.ts` / `__probe.test.ts` (04-check-method.md stack profile, M9 lint). The corrected code below ran in a scratch tree: the real tools/shared, the real tsconfig.node.json options, a stub `spec-pipeline/protocol` that re-exports the real `PausePayload`, `EXIT_OK` and `EXIT_STEP_FAILED`, W2-05's `irSet` and W2-04's fake as their briefs describe them. Result: tsc clean, eslint clean, 9 tests green.
4	
5	| # | Sev | Item | Problem | Evidence | Proposed change |
6	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
7	| 1 | high | D3, D4 (C3, C8) | edited goals can never be confirmed from the screen. `w` returns `edit`, and applyResolve writes goals.json but not confirmed.json. The flow resumes, resolve-confirm pauses again (its output is missing), and the C8 re-pause guard sends the person to the operator; a third pause → exit 4 | 02-contracts.md C3: "`confirmed.json` … its existence completes the step"; C8: "If the same step pauses again right after its action, dpf runs the operator"; briefs/W2-08.md:86-87,93-97 | `w` keeps the edits and returns to the main content, which shows the edited goals; `a` returns `accept` carrying the writes; applyResolve runs the writes, then copies the template. The plan owner decides; if an edit should instead re-show the screen without resuming, C8 and W2-13 need that rule |
8	| 2 | high | D2, D3 | the walk duplicates every goal. The initial state's goals are `input.goals.goals`, and keep/replace append to them, so T3 yields `[G-1, G-2, G-1, G-2']`: T3's exact value fails, and ir refuses the duplicate ids | briefs/W2-08.md:74-75,81,84-85; resolution.ts:32-33 `id "…" is used more than once` | the walk records one decision per entry (kept, replaced or dropped) and builds the lists from them at `w` (corrected code) |
9	| 3 | high | D4, TESTS | T3 cannot pass. The fake's plan has a single `{ exit: 0 }` entry, but D4 spawns twice (irSet, then irValidate). The second call reads `plan[1]` = undefined → TypeError → exit 1, irValidate is not ok, and applyResolve throws. irValidate is also EXTRA: `ir set` parses the whole document before it writes, and C11 and the row say one irSet | briefs/W2-08.md:96,134-135; W2-04 D2 step 1 `entry = plan[n]`; spec-pipeline/src/ir/command.ts:242-244 `parseIrWith(IR_KINDS[edit.kind], …)` before `writeIr` | no irValidate; one plan entry per write |
10	| 4 | high | TESTS | T3 asserts G-2's source in calls.jsonl, but irSet passes the value as `--value @<tmp>` and deletes the temp file in a `finally`; the fake records argv only | briefs/W2-08.md:142-143; W2-05 D1:46-48; W2-04 D2 step 4 | the screen test asserts the values in the result; the applyResolve test asserts the argv per write (value `@…`) and the template copy. Residual: an applyResolve that forwards a wrong value still passes — no unit sink sees the temp file |
11	| 5 | high | TESTS | `'../src/screens/resolve-confirm.js'` from tools/dpf/tests/screens/ resolves to tools/dpf/tests/src/… | briefs/W2-08.md:133 | `'../../src/screens/resolve-confirm.js'` |
12	| 6 | high | D2, D4 | the import lines fail simple-import-sort (an error): the specifiers are unsorted, and node:fs comes after the relative imports | probe: `1:1 error Run autofix to sort these imports! simple-import-sort/imports` | the import block of the corrected code |
